@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Income Tax Ordinance [New Version] (פקודת מס הכנסה [נוסח חדש]), ss 120B, 121 and 121B.
-- THE NOUNS: DECLARE and nothing else. Every rule module imports this one.
--
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/income-tax-ordinance-new-version.he.wiki.txt,
-- Hebrew Wikisource raw MediaWiki, retrieved 2026-10-06, sha256 b87f2cf4...6b81b6.
-- An unofficial consolidation of the text as amended at retrieval. A `src:N` comment
-- quotes line N of that file, copied mechanically; nothing in Hebrew here is typed by hand.
--
-- Money is new Israeli shekels (NIS), as a bare NUMBER, for a whole tax year.
-- Membership test for this module: a witness of ordinary competence could testify to the
-- fact, or a register or a return records it. Whether the fact makes tax payable is a
-- rule, and belongs in the section module that says so.

§ `Nouns for sections 120B, 121 and 121B`

§§ `An item of the individual's income`

-- One item of the individual's taxable income for the tax year.
-- src:117 | ”הכנסה חייבת“ – הכנסה לאחר הניכויים, הקיזוזים והפטורים שהותרו ממנה לפי כל דין;
--
-- INPUT CONVENTIONS, each because the rule that settles the question is outside this row:
-- * `amount` is the item as it stands AFTER any spreading under s 8(c) that the taxpayer
--   requested; s 121B(d) applies s 8(c) for s 121B too (see ito-121b-additional-tax.l4).
-- * The items are those charged to THIS individual. Whether a spouse's income is computed
--   separately or with the registered spouse is s 66 (row IL-02).
-- * `from personal exertion` classifies the item under the s 1 definition, which is
--   inclusive ("לרבות") and so not closed:
-- src:170 | ”הכנסה מיגיעה אישית“ – לרבות –
-- * `charged at the rates in section 121` is FALSE for an item that another section
--   charges at a rate of its own (capital gain under s 91, rent under s 122, dividend under
--   s 125B, interest under s 125C, and the rest). Those sections are not in this row; the
--   item still counts as taxable income for s 121B.
DECLARE `An item of income` HAS
    `amount`                                                               IS A NUMBER
    `from personal exertion`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `charged at the rates in section 121`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `subject to a duty to keep books of account, and acceptable books were not kept` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`                        IS A NUMBER

-- `under section 2(1) or 2(2)`: business or vocation (s 2(1)), employment (s 2(2)).
-- src:4464 | (1) הכנסה לפי סעיף 2(1) או (2);
-- `subject to a duty ...`: the facts s 121(b)(2) turns on. "Acceptable books" is defined
-- by what the assessing officer, a s 146 committee or a court decided, which a return or a
-- register records:
-- src:192 | ”פנקסים קבילים“ – פנקסי חשבונות שפקיד השומה לא סירב לקבלם ולא פסל אותם, או שסירב לקבלם או פסלם אולם ועדה כאמור בסעיף 146 או בית המשפט ביטלו את החלטתו ובלבד שלא יראו פנקסים כקבילים אם הנישום הודה כי אינם קבילים ואישר בכתב שהוסברו לו התוצאות המשפטיות הנובעות מהודאתו;
-- `inflationary amount, as defined in section 88`: the part of a capital gain that s 88
-- calls inflationary; 0 for an item that is not a capital gain. s 121B(e) excludes it.

§§ `A sale of a right in real estate`

-- s 121B(e) counts betterment (שבח) under the Real Estate Taxation (Betterment, Sale and
-- Purchase) Law 5723-1963 as taxable income, less its inflationary amount under s 47 of
-- that Law, and, for a residential apartment, only above a sale-value threshold and only
-- where the sale is not exempt. Each of these is computed or decided under that Law, which
-- is not in this row, and is recorded on the assessment of the sale: so each is an input.
-- src:4462 | ”הכנסה חייבת“ – הכנסה חייבת כהגדרתה בסעיף 1 וכמשמעותה בסעיף 89, למעט סכום אינפלציוני כהגדרתו בסעיף 88 וסכום אינפלציוני כהגדרתו בסעיף 47 לחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, ולרבות שבח כמשמעותו בחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, ואולם לגבי מכירת זכות במקרקעין בדירת מגורים כהגדרתה בחוק האמור – רק אם שווי מכירתה עולה על 5,385,285 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2025; בשנת 2026, 5,385,285 ש״ח)] והמכירה אינה פטורה ממס לפי כל דין; הסכום האמור יתואם בהתאם להוראות סעיף 9(ג2) לחוק מיסוי מקרקעין, ולעניין זה יהיה המדד הבסיסי כאמור באותו סעיף המדד שפורסם ביום המדד שפורסם ביום ז׳ בשבט התשפ״ז (15 בינואר 2027);
DECLARE `A sale of a right in real estate` HAS
    `betterment`                                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `inflationary amount, as defined in section 47 of the Real Estate Taxation Law` IS A NUMBER
    `in a residential apartment`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `sale value`                                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `exempt from tax under any law`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `The individual in a tax year`

-- The case. `tax year` is a calendar year: s 1 defines a tax year as twelve months from
-- 1 January, OR a special assessment period where one has been set. Special assessment
-- periods are not modelled (NOTES.md, fork F12).
-- src:202 | ”שנת מס“ – תקופה של שנים עשר חדשים רצופים, שתחילתה ב־1 בינואר, ואם נקבעה תקופת שומה מיוחדת – תקופת השומה שנקבעה כאמור;
DECLARE `An individual in a tax year` HAS
    `tax year`                       IS A NUMBER
    `date of birth`                  IS A DATE
    `items of income`                IS A LIST OF `An item of income`
    `sales of rights in real estate` IS A LIST OF `A sale of a right in real estate`

§§ `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B`

-- Invalid input is rejected, not answered (EITHER, left side): the caller can fix it.
-- Version 0.2.0 (repair 03-N4): named for the sections that use it. In 0.1.0 it was
-- `A problem with the facts`, a name row IL-06 also declares (capstone RECONCILE.md, N4), so
-- that no module could import both rows and name either type. The constructors are unchanged.
DECLARE `A problem with the facts, for sections 121 and 121B` IS ONE OF
    `an amount of income is negative`
    `an inflationary amount is negative`
    `a betterment or a sale value is negative`

§§ `The income ceilings of section 121`

-- "Income ceilings" (תקרות הכנסה) is a term of s 120A, the definitions of Part 6.1, which
-- is not in this row but which tells s 120B what it adjusts:
-- src:4335 | ”תקרות הכנסה“ – סכומי ההכנסה לענין קביעת שיעורי המס על פי סעיף 121, וכן הכנסה החייבת במס נוסף, כמשמעותה בסעיף 121ב.
-- The six s 121 ceilings, each the TOP of a marginal band, named for the band and not for
-- the paragraph. The rates themselves are not indexed and are not here; they are printed
-- in the rule (ito-121-individual-rates.l4).
--   (a)(1) `top of the 31% band`               (a)(2) `top of the 35% band`
--   (b)(1)(a) `top of the reduced-rate 10% band`  (b)(1)(b) `top of the reduced-rate 14% band`
--   (b)(1)(c) `top of the reduced-rate 20% band`  (b)(1)(d) `top of the reduced-rate 31% band`
-- The s 121B(a) amount is the seventh income ceiling. It is not in this record because the
-- text prints it at a different base year (2017) and its in-force figure is an input.
DECLARE `The income ceilings of section 121` HAS
    `top of the 31% band`              IS A NUMBER
    `top of the 35% band`              IS A NUMBER
    `top of the reduced-rate 10% band` IS A NUMBER
    `top of the reduced-rate 14% band` IS A NUMBER
    `top of the reduced-rate 20% band` IS A NUMBER
    `top of the reduced-rate 31% band` IS A NUMBER

§§ `The index and the amounts that s 120B adjusts`

-- The consumer price index published by the Central Bureau of Statistics:
-- src:179 | ”מדד“ – מדד המחירים לצרכן שמפרסמת הלשכה המרכזית לסטטיסטיקה;
-- s 1 defines the rate of increase over a period by two PUBLISHED readings, not by the
-- months they measure; which publication was last before each edge is a fact about the
-- Bureau's calendar, so the caller supplies the two readings:
-- src:180 | ”שיעור עליית המדד“, בתקופה פלונית – ההפרש בין המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני סוף התקופה לבין המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני תחילת התקופה, מחולק במדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני תחילת התקופה;
-- No default and no figure is supplied in this row: the index is published by the Bureau,
-- and no publication of it was fetched (NOTES.md section 7).
DECLARE `Index readings for a period` HAS
    `index last published before the start of the period` IS A NUMBER
    `index last published before the end of the period`   IS A NUMBER

-- The five kinds of amount s 120B(a) adjusts ("לכל אלה ייקרא בסעיף זה – הסכומים"):
-- src:4338 | (א) ב־1 בינואר של כל שנת מס יתואמו תקרות ההכנסה, סכומי נקודת זיכוי ונקודת קיצבה וכן ההנחות הסוציאליות וסכומי התרומה המוכרים (לכל אלה ייקרא בסעיף זה – הסכומים), שהיו ב־1 בינואר של שנת המס הקודמת, לפי שיעור עליית המדד בשנת המס הקודמת.
DECLARE `A kind of amount adjusted under section 120B` IS ONE OF
    `an income ceiling`                -- תקרות ההכנסה (s 120A)
    `the amount of a credit point`     -- סכומי נקודת זיכוי (ss 33A-36A, row IL-01)
    `the amount of an allowance point` -- נקודת קיצבה; the only kind s 120B(b) also adjusts mid-year
    `a social deduction`               -- ההנחות הסוציאליות (s 120A)
    `a recognised donation amount`     -- סכומי התרומה המוכרים (s 120A)

-- The facts needed to say what one amount is on 1 January of a tax year. Each figure is
-- published by the Israel Tax Authority or computed from published index readings; none
-- has a default here.
-- * `amount on 1 January of the previous tax year, before rounding`: the base s 120B(a)
--   adjusts. Fork F6 (NOTES.md) is whether the chain carries rounded or unrounded figures.
-- * `readings for the previous tax year`: the s 1 readings for the previous tax year.
-- * the two 1 January 2024 figures are the ones s 120B(e) freezes and restarts from.
--   Version 0.2.0 (repair 03-O2, INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md observation O2): the figure BEFORE
--   rounding is a MAYBE. The Tax Authority publishes the rounded figure; a caller who holds
--   only that one passes NOTHING here, and the 2028 adjustment, the one rule that reads this
--   field, declines by name. In 0.1.0 the field was a NUMBER, so a rounded figure put in it
--   gave a plausible 2028 amount with no diagnostic.
DECLARE `An amount on 1 January of a tax year` HAS
    `kind`                                                          IS A `A kind of amount adjusted under section 120B`
    `tax year`                                                      IS A NUMBER
    `amount on 1 January of the previous tax year, before rounding` IS A NUMBER
    `readings for the previous tax year`                            IS AN `Index readings for a period`
    `amount on 1 January 2024, before rounding`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `amount on 1 January 2024, after rounding`                      IS A NUMBER

-- s 120B(b): a cost-of-living increment agreed between the Coordination Bureau of Economic
-- Organisations and the Histadrut, for work done from a given month onward.
-- src:4339 | (ב) נקבע בהסכם בין לשכת התיאום של הארגונים הכלכליים לבין ההסתדרות הכללית של העובדים בארץ ישראל, כי תשולם תוספת יוקר לשכירים במשק, לגבי עבודה שבוצעה בחודש פלוני ואילך, יתואמו באותו חודש סכומי נקודת הקיצבה שהיו ב־1 בינואר של שנת המס, לפי שיעור עליית המדד מתחילת שנת המס עד תום החודש האמור.
-- `month from which an agreed cost-of-living increment is paid`: NOTHING where no such
-- agreement was made in the tax year (the provision contemplates its own absence).
-- Version 0.2.0 (repair 01-W5): "נקודת קיצבה" is rendered "allowance point", as row IL-01
-- renders it where s 33A defines it (line 1564) and row IL-08 renders it in s 40; 0.1.0 said
-- "pension point". The choice is the lead's, 2026-10-08, assumed, not ruled (NOTES.md,
-- "Version 0.2.0"). The names renamed: `the amount of a pension point`,
-- `A pension-point amount in a tax year`, and in ito-120b-indexation.l4
-- `s 120B(b) — the pension-point amount from the month of an agreed cost-of-living increment`.
DECLARE `An allowance-point amount in a tax year` HAS
    `tax year`                                                    IS A NUMBER
    `amount on 1 January of the tax year`                         IS A NUMBER
    `month from which an agreed cost-of-living increment is paid` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `readings from the start of the tax year to the end of that month` IS AN `Index readings for a period`

-- What s 120B makes of an amount for a tax year. Two outcomes the text names, one with a
-- payload each: a frozen year has a figure fixed by (e)(1), already rounded; any other year
-- has an adjusted figure that the s 120B(d) rounding rules then round.
DECLARE `The amount for a tax year under section 120B` IS ONE OF
    `fixed by section 120B(e)(1) at` HAS `the amount after rounding`  IS A NUMBER
    `adjusted, before rounding, to`  HAS `the amount before rounding` IS A NUMBER
